  "files": [
    {
      "fileName": "blind-fight.json",
      "id": "y2XeMe1F18lIyo59",
      "name": "Blind-Fight",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "y2XeMe1F18lIyo59",
        "folder": "fyeZAb6UU0hj94Ck",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Blind-Fight",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Fighter, Rogue, Investigator</strong> Your battle instincts make you more aware of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Concealed] and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Invisible] opponents.</p>\n<p><strong>Ranger</strong> Your heightened senses allow you to instinctively detect unseen opponents.</p><hr /><p>You don't need to succeed at a flat check to target concealed creatures. You're not @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] to creatures that are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Hidden] from you (unless you're off-guard to them for reasons other than the hidden condition), and you need only a successful @Check[flat|showDC:all|dc:5] to target a hidden creature.</p>\n<p>While you're adjacent to an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Undetected] creature of your level or lower, it is instead only hidden from you.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "master in Perception"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "fighter",
              "investigator",
              "ranger",
              "rogue"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "cant-you-see.json",
      "id": "9sl2t3jb5ZdQA3K4",
      "name": "Can't You See?",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "9sl2t3jb5ZdQA3K4",
        "folder": "fyeZAb6UU0hj94Ck",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Can't You See?",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The eye rebels, the mind recoils—no matter how much those who can see you try to explain what's there, their friends' gazes just skitter over you, like a bird afraid to land. A character who attempts to Point Out your location must attempt a @Check[flat|dc:14]. If they fail, their allies misunderstand them and aren't sure where you are. On a critical failure, their allies think they pointed you out in a different location entirely, chosen by the GM. Similarly, when a creature critically fails to [[/act seek]] you while you're @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Hidden] to or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Undetected] by it, it thinks you're in a different location chosen by the GM. In either case, you appear to be hidden to a creature that thinks you're in a different location, though you're actually undetected by it for targeting and further uses of the Seek action.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "trained in Occultism"
              },
              {
                "value": "expert in Stealth"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Dark Archive (Remastered)"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "druid",
              "ranger"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "eerie-environs.json",
      "id": "po0WNUVwtaEBK8LH",
      "name": "Eerie Environs",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "po0WNUVwtaEBK8LH",
        "folder": "fyeZAb6UU0hj94Ck",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Eerie Environs",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The natural world can be scary to those not used to it—and you make it scarier still. If you're @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Hidden] from a creature, you can attempt to [[/act demoralize]] it without losing your hidden condition—imitating the sounds of strange beasts or causing the foliage to rustle menacingly. When you do so, you don't take a penalty to your check if the target doesn't understand your language.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "trained in Intimidation"
              },
              {
                "value": "trained in Stealth"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Dark Archive (Remastered)"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "druid",
              "ranger"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "eerie-traces.json",
      "id": "BaKEnNbzbGlenmRv",
      "name": "Eerie Traces",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "BaKEnNbzbGlenmRv",
        "folder": "fyeZAb6UU0hj94Ck",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Eerie Traces",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The tracks you leave behind are strange, somehow disconcerting and unnerving—they might travel backward, or through places no one would think to pass through. You change your tracks into eerie traces, moving up to half your travel speed as you do so. You don't need to attempt a Survival check to change your tracks, but anyone tracking you must attempt a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The tracker is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The tracker becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 1} for as long as it follows your tracks. This condition doesn't decrease until the tracker stops following you, and it comes back if the tracker resumes following your tracks. If the tracker enters into an encounter with you after following your tracks, it begins the encounter frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but your disturbing traces cause the tracker to be @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 2} instead.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "trained in Intimidation"
              },
              {
                "value": "trained in Survival"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Dark Archive (Remastered)"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "concentrate",
              "druid",
              "exploration",
              "move",
              "ranger"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
